CPU-time clocks of threads and processes: pthread_getcpuclockid and
clock_getcpuclockid give the id of a thread's or a process's CPU-time
clock through the GetThreadCpuclockid and GetCpuclockid sysdeps, and
clock_gettime and clock_getres then take the id. They always failed, with
ENOENT and ENOSYS, so a program could not ask how much CPU time another
thread or process had used. The ids are a system's to make, from its own
numbers for threads and processes; a system without the sysdeps keeps the
old answers, without the log line. Meant for upstream.

